          "id": "q2_opt_3",
          "slot_position": 3,
          "label_markdown": "$25x^{5}$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "id": "q2_opt_4",
          "slot_position": 4,
          "label_markdown": "$5x^{5}$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "answer_key": [
        "q2_opt_1"
      ],
      "explanation_markdown": "**Given.** $f(x) = 5x^{5}$.\n\n**Rule — the power rule.** $$\\dfrac{d}{dx}x^n = n\\,x^{n-1}.$$\n\n**Step 1 — Bring the power down as a multiplier.** Multiply the coefficient by $n = 5$: $\\;5\\times5 = 25$.\n\n**Step 2 — Reduce the power by one.** The exponent becomes $5 - 1 = 4$, giving $$f'(x) = 25x^{4}.$$\n\n**Answer.** $f'(x) = 25x^{4}$.",
      "source_style_ref": "CBSE Class 12 Mathematics, Differentiation (parametrised)"
    },
